hadiths[38]{hadithnumber,text}:
"431","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever becomes bankrupt among the people and a man finds his own wealth (present) in exactly the same condition, then he has more right to that wealth than anyone else."
"432","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys an animal whose udder has been withheld (from milking), if he returns it, he should return with it one sa’ of dates."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Not wheat."
"433","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys such an animal (like a she-camel, cow, or goat, etc.) whose milk has been withheld, then he milks it, he has a choice: if he wishes, he may keep it, and if he wishes, he may return it, and along with it, he should give one sa’ (approximately two and a quarter kilograms) of dates."
"434","Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) similar to the previous hadith: and he said: ""Milk it three times."
"435","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys a she-camel or a goat whose udders have been tied up (to accumulate milk), and then he milks it, he has the right to choose between two options: if he wishes, he may keep it, and if he wishes, he may return it and give along with it a container full of grain."" ‘Awf narrated: This is when there is a deficiency in its milk. Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said the same."
"436","Muawiyah al-Mahdi narrated, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: O Mahdi! The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the earnings of the cupper, the price of a dog, the earnings of the flute player’s profession, and the earnings from mating a bull."
"437","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not bid over the bid of his (Muslim) brother until he buys or leaves it; a man should not propose marriage over the proposal of his brother until he marries or receives a response; a woman should not demand the divorce of her (Muslim) sister so that she may empty her plate (vessel), for a Muslim woman is the sister of a Muslim woman."
"438","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A townsman should not sell for a villager, nor should a man bid against his brother’s price, nor should he send a marriage proposal over his brother’s proposal. Do not artificially raise prices merely to increase the price (bidding). A woman should not demand the divorce of her (Muslim) sister so that she may obtain what is in her vessel; she will only get what is decreed for her. And do not withhold milk in the udders of camels and goats. So, whoever buys such an animal whose milk has been withheld, he has the choice of two options: if he returns it, then he should return it with one sa’ (approximately two and a quarter kilograms) of dates. An animal held as collateral may be ridden and its milk may be drunk."
"439","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) forbade that a townsman should sell on behalf of a villager. The narrator said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): What is meant by your statement, ""A townsman should not sell on behalf of a villager""? He replied: That he should not become his agent (broker)."
"440","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us, and he praised and glorified Allah. Then he mentioned betrayal and explained its severity. Then he said: ""O people! I should not find any one of you..."" Then the narrator narrated the rest of the hadith similar to the narration of Jarir (which comes later)."
"441","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""I should not find any of you on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that he has a camel on his neck and it is groaning."" Then the narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith up to its end in similar words, but did not mention its first part."
"442","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade earnings from the prostitution of slave women."
"443","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade earnings from slave women."
"444","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies leaving wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves a debt, it is upon us."
"445","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade meeting trading caravans on the way before they reach the market, bidding merely to raise the price, and withholding the milk of milking animals. He also forbade that a woman demand the divorce of her (Muslim) sister, and that a man bid over the price set by his (Muslim) brother."
"446","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Silver should be exchanged for silver in equal amounts and by weight, so whatever is in excess is usury. And gold should be exchanged for gold in equal amounts and by weight, so whatever is in excess is usury. And dates should not be sold until their (ripeness) becomes apparent."
"447","A man from the people of Madinah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys stolen goods while knowing that they are stolen, then he is equally a partner in its disgrace and sin."
"448","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys stolen goods knowing that they are stolen, then he is equally a partner in its disgrace and sin."
"449","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Two types of sales are bad: the sale of food and the sale of slaves."
"450","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) forbade auctioning in things other than inheritance, partnership, and the sale of spoils."
"451","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade two types of clothing and two types of sales: wrapping a sheet around the body in such a way that it becomes difficult to move the hands and arms, and sitting in a single garment in such a manner that there is a risk of the private parts becoming exposed; and he forbade the sales of Mulamasa and Munabadhah."
"452","Lady Rabi’ bint Mu’awwiz ibn ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I, along with some women of the Ansar, went to Asma’ bint Mukhrabah, the mother of Abu Jahl. Her son, ‘Ayyash bin ‘Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah, used to send perfume to her from Yemen, and she would sell it to those who received a monthly allowance. I bought perfume from her, and she weighed it for me. I put it into my bottles, just as she had weighed it for the woman next to me. She said to me: Write down for me what you owe me. I said to her: Write it down as a debt on Rabi’ bint Mu’awwiz ibn ‘Afra’. She said: You are the daughter of the killer of her chief. I said: By Allah! I am not the killer, but I am the daughter of the killer of her slave. She said: By Allah! I will never sell this to you. I said: By Allah! I will never buy anything from you. By Allah! It is not even a fragrance. Then she said: Daughter! By Allah! I have never smelled a fragrance better than this, but at the time when she said what she said, I became angry, and so I said what I said."
"453","It is narrated from Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave her a share of forty wasq of dates and twenty wasq of barley in Khaybar. Asim bin Adi came to her and said: If I give you the same thing here in Madinah and take it from you in Khaybar, she replied: I will ask the Commander of the Faithful, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). She mentioned this to him, and he disliked it and said: What will happen to the guarantee? Wakee’ (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is hundi (a type of promissory note), and it is disliked."
"454","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever buys grain should not sell it until he measures it."" I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Why? He said: Do you not see that they used to sell it for gold coins while there was only hope of the grain arriving?"
"455","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of anything before taking possession of it, and that is only regarding grain. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I consider everything to be in the same position as grain."
"456","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever buys grain should not sell it until he takes possession of it."" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: I consider everything to be in the same position as grain."
"457","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade meeting trading caravans on the way before they reach the market."
"458","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: We used to cultivate land on the basis of sharecropping and did not see any harm in it, until Sayyiduna Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade it."
"459","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If any of you gives a piece of land to his (Muslim) brother without compensation, it is better for him than taking a fixed rent from him."
"460","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: ‘Umra is for the one for whom ‘Umra is made, Ruqba is for the one for whom Ruqba is made. And the one who takes back his gift is like the one who licks up his own vomit."
"461","Syedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Madinah, the people there used to sell fruits in advance for one, two, or three years. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells dates in advance (salam), let him do so for a specified measure and a specified period."
"462","Ibn Abi Najih narrated with this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"463","Ibn Abi Najih narrated from this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"464","Abu Al-Minhāl narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) a narration similar to this."
"465","Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A partner is a mediator (has the right of pre-emption), and pre-emption is in everything."" Ata, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It (pre-emption) is only in land, so Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: No, what do you know?"
"466","Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Pre-emption applies to a slave and to everything."
"467","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The partner has the right of pre-emption, and pre-emption is in everything."
"468","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, his armor was mortgaged with a Jewish man in exchange for thirty sa’ of barley, which he had taken for food for his family."
